{"id": "s2-W7-0320", "decision": "fix_clean", "clean": "Okay, so the Sprocket mobile app needs offline support. The main flows are viewing the task list, editing a task, and creating a task. When offline, the changes should be saved locally in SQLite and queued, and when the connection comes back we replay the queue in order against the API. Conflicts are resolved with last write wins, using the updated timestamp from the server. Show a small banner when the app is offline and a spinner badge on tasks that have pending changes. Please don't build everything at once. Start with the local database layer and the queue, write tests for them, and stop so I can review.", "reason": "dropped_by_recognizer", "rules": ["RECOVER"], "note": "'at' of updated_at lost; raw says 'updated timestamp'"}
